    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "The glazing serving the additional three side windows at first floor, as seen along the proposed north elevation of the development indicated on drawing No. 009, shall be in obscured glass with an equivalent obscuration as level 3 on the Pilkington Obscuration Range and the window shall be non-opening unless the parts of the window which can be opened are more than 1.7 metres above the floor of the room in which the window is installed. The glazing shall not be altered without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining and neighbouring properties\r"
